From 52ee56b787f1364e3b678e130cf7939acef1c4f3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 07:32:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] player information: what to do when the converter of the
 board is turned off, or not on the list

A Dolby Vision video that does not go out as Dolby Vision because of the
DisplayPort to HDMI converter of the board (DV_CONVERTER::Decide(),
videoscreen.hadesdvconverter) had a reason on the overview and no advice
for two of its three cases: the converter turned off in the settings
(converteroff), and a board that is not on the list of those where Dolby
Vision was seen working through it (converterunlisted). TodoForReason()
gave them nothing.

converteroff now says to set "Dolby Vision through a display converter"
back to Automatic in the display settings (converteron); converterunlisted
says to try it with On, and to set it back to Automatic if the picture
goes (convertertry), as the help of the setting says. Estuary's strings
32748 and 32749, in English and in the three Spanish files, read as
$ADDON[skin.estuary n]; the pages of Hades for other skins made again from
Estuary's (tools/hades-playerinfo).
